WEBVTT

00:03.002 --> 00:05.463
The time has finally come!

00:05.547 --> 00:10.093
I will now introduce you the final event
of Day Three of the Founder's Festival!

00:10.176 --> 00:17.183
We are about to show you a small portion
of Tempest's proud impregnable dungeon!

00:18.101 --> 00:18.935
There!

00:28.028 --> 00:32.741
This is the ultimate challenge for adventurers,
presented by our leader, the Demon Lord Rimuru!

00:32.824 --> 00:37.328
Will anybody out there
be able to conquer it?!

00:37.537 --> 00:40.915
<i>This will be one of the centerpieces
of our nation's future development.</i>

00:40.999 --> 00:42.333
<i>I'm counting on you guys.</i>

02:13.007 --> 02:13.842
Without further ado, allow me
to introduce our challengers!

02:13.925 --> 02:17.303
(Episode 71: The Labyrinth's Grand Opening)

02:17.387 --> 02:21.850
Our first group is Team
Great Lightning led by Basson!

02:22.016 --> 02:25.687
You can try to intimidate us,
but we won't fall for that!

02:25.770 --> 02:28.648
Yeah! Basson's right!

02:29.858 --> 02:32.443
You're not forgetting about me, are you?

02:32.527 --> 02:34.445
Don't be that way, Gomez!

02:34.529 --> 02:36.990
They know all about how strong you are.

02:37.365 --> 02:42.495
As long as you and I are together, our
Team Great Lightning got nothing to fear!

02:42.787 --> 02:44.289
What's up with those guys?

02:44.706 --> 02:46.749
But oh well, at least they seems fun.

02:47.083 --> 02:49.294
Next on is a group of familiar faces.

02:49.377 --> 02:52.797
The three besties of
Eren, Kaval, and Gido!

02:52.881 --> 02:54.883
Are we really doing this?

02:55.258 --> 02:57.051
Of course we are!

02:57.135 --> 03:01.598
We haven't had any real adventures
lately, so I've been waiting for this!

03:01.764 --> 03:07.020
Just to be sure, as the leader, I do
have the right to say no, right? Right?

03:07.103 --> 03:08.313
Of course you don't!

03:08.396 --> 03:10.607
This is already set in stone!

03:10.690 --> 03:12.734
Eren!

03:12.817 --> 03:14.944
Didn't you say you were
going to visit home?!

03:15.028 --> 03:16.362
Quiet.

03:17.572 --> 03:19.782
I didn't expect those
three to show up, too.

03:20.116 --> 03:23.077
And our third group
need no introduction!

03:23.161 --> 03:26.748
It's the Lightspeed Hero and his party!

03:26.915 --> 03:30.501
Will he carve another legend
like in the Battle Tournament?!

03:30.585 --> 03:32.670
Masayuki! Masayuki! Masayuki!
Masayuki! Masayuki! Masayuki!

03:32.837 --> 03:36.132
Good. Seems like he was
able to convince his friends.

03:36.341 --> 03:37.967
Will they be okay?

03:38.051 --> 03:39.969
I gave him a map for the dungeon.

03:40.053 --> 03:42.555
I'm sure he'll help advertise
the dungeon just fine.

03:42.931 --> 03:45.058
Now, let us begin right awa-

03:45.141 --> 03:46.184
Halt!

03:48.770 --> 03:50.772
I'll join in, too.

03:54.150 --> 03:58.196
You've done well trapping me
in your silly bluffs, I must say.

03:58.488 --> 04:00.573
Ugh, not that guy again.

04:02.325 --> 04:05.912
The Demon Lord's Big Four or whatever
certainly play dirty, do they not?

04:06.496 --> 04:10.708
Scheme all you want, but I'll
crush your ambitions for good!

04:10.792 --> 04:13.795
How dare he be so rude towards
Great Rimuru. Unforgivable.

04:13.878 --> 04:15.797
I'll get to him and shut his mou-

04:15.880 --> 04:16.798
Don't.

04:17.173 --> 04:18.091
Yes, sir.

04:18.883 --> 04:21.219
Let us now begin!

04:21.302 --> 04:28.017
The progress of each parties will be
shown live through these large screens!

04:31.938 --> 04:35.858
The four dryads here are
the managers of this dungeon.

04:35.942 --> 04:42.282
This time each one of them will accompany
each party to give guidance on the dungeon!

04:42.824 --> 04:45.285
I will now explain the rules!

04:45.618 --> 04:48.579
First, I'm going to
give these to everyone!

04:48.788 --> 04:50.707
Please look at the screen.

04:50.790 --> 04:55.128
These are items we're planning to offer for
sale when the dungeon is officially open.

04:55.378 --> 04:57.714
This item is called the
Resurrection Bracelet.

04:57.797 --> 05:02.218
We highly recommend you purchase
this when you enter our dungeon.

05:02.885 --> 05:06.347
Believe it or not,
it resurrects you from the dead!

05:06.431 --> 05:07.932
That can't be true!

05:08.016 --> 05:09.017
Impossible!

05:09.100 --> 05:11.060
Please calm down!

05:11.144 --> 05:14.272
This part is important,
so please listen properly.

05:14.355 --> 05:19.527
This item only works if
you are inside our dungeon.

05:19.610 --> 05:22.905
Please be aware that this
doesn't work elsewhere.

05:24.073 --> 05:26.409
You won't die inside the dungeon, you say?

05:26.492 --> 05:29.162
If that's true, then
<i>you</i> should show us!

05:29.245 --> 05:31.080
Oh, me?

05:31.289 --> 05:34.876
That's an understandable suggestion,
so I'd be happy to.

05:34.959 --> 05:38.254
As expected from Sir Mjöllmile.
He did not flinch in a slightest.

05:38.337 --> 05:40.673
He already experienced it before, after all.

05:40.757 --> 05:43.051
Though, he was scared at first, of course.

05:46.512 --> 05:47.805
All right.

05:47.889 --> 05:49.348
See ya!

05:52.351 --> 05:54.812
I will now actually attack Mjöllmile in here-

05:54.896 --> 05:56.314
I won't fall for your trick!

06:02.820 --> 06:04.489
He purposely playing with him!

06:04.572 --> 06:05.406
So mean!

06:05.782 --> 06:07.283
I'll give you the final blow.

06:14.123 --> 06:17.251
And there you have it!
I'm back in perfect shape!

06:18.211 --> 06:19.337
It's a miracle!

06:19.420 --> 06:24.342
This bracelet actually also have
a pain-reducing effect!

06:24.425 --> 06:27.470
<i>That was a pretty
unpleasant role I had him do.</i>

06:27.553 --> 06:29.555
<i>I should thank him
with something latter.</i>

06:29.722 --> 06:32.475
<i>Still, that Gaiye bastard...!</i>

06:33.184 --> 06:36.562
The dungeon exploration has finally began!

06:36.646 --> 06:38.648
From here on out is a brand-new world.

06:38.731 --> 06:42.527
What could be awaiting
these brave challengers?

06:44.612 --> 06:48.241
Tch, it's the same damn
kind of corridor over and over!

06:48.324 --> 06:50.535
Nothing but crossroads!

06:51.160 --> 06:54.288
Weren't we at this
intersection before, boss?

06:54.372 --> 06:56.874
Oh come on! At least
draw a map or something!

06:56.958 --> 07:00.044
Do these guys always go out
without a plan like this?

07:00.128 --> 07:03.840
This is bad news! This dungeon
thing is bigger than I thought.

07:03.923 --> 07:08.469
What are you people? Idiots?
That Demon Lord's just feeding us a tall tale.

07:08.553 --> 07:11.848
I bet he's using magic or
something to disorient us.

07:11.931 --> 07:13.099
I-I see!

07:13.182 --> 07:14.809
You sure knows a lot, Basson!

07:15.059 --> 07:16.602
These guys are no good.

07:17.019 --> 07:20.148
Let's break through
this spell right away...

07:25.695 --> 07:29.240
Wh-Whoa! Was that a trapdoor?

07:29.323 --> 07:30.158
Hm?

07:30.241 --> 07:33.411
Did I add trapdoors in Floor 1?

07:34.704 --> 07:35.830
Ramiris?

07:36.664 --> 07:38.249
Yes? What is it, sir?

07:38.332 --> 07:41.544
Well, just wanna ask about
the floor I prepared.

07:42.128 --> 07:44.547
You didn't tinker with it without
my permission, didn't you?

07:45.923 --> 07:51.929
W-Well, actually, we wanted to make the
labyrinth a more complete creation, so...

07:52.013 --> 07:53.890
How many trapdoors did you add?

07:53.973 --> 07:56.434
A-A decent number of them...

07:56.517 --> 08:00.688
Are you serious?! There's no need
for trapdoors in the top floors!

08:00.771 --> 08:03.816
The top floors are meant to
get people lost and tire them out.

08:03.900 --> 08:06.277
All the trapdoors
will just be shortcuts.

08:06.360 --> 08:10.239
But there were more fiendish
trapdoors in the lower levels, right?

08:10.323 --> 08:13.576
So I thought perhaps you
forgot to install some higher up.

08:13.659 --> 08:16.078
I just did it out of kindness, I swear

08:16.162 --> 08:17.663
I didn't need that type of kindness!

08:18.706 --> 08:20.958
Team Kaval appears to be doing well.

08:21.042 --> 08:24.504
They properly write down stuff as they progress.
A textbook example of dungeon exploration.

08:24.587 --> 08:25.880
I believe it's over here.

08:27.798 --> 08:30.843
They already got their
third treasure chest!

08:31.302 --> 08:34.055
Oh? They sure are progressing smoothly.

08:34.388 --> 08:38.893
They didn't hit any trapdoors, and they're
dodging the traps I set up as well.

08:40.770 --> 08:41.771
Hey, Ramiris.

08:41.854 --> 08:43.648
Wh-What is it, sir?

08:44.065 --> 08:46.192
I have my trust in you, okay?

08:46.275 --> 08:48.736
You won't keep secrets
from me, won't you?

08:48.819 --> 08:51.072
Yeah, of course, Rimuru!

08:51.155 --> 08:54.867
So let me ask, did you do
something to Eren's group?

08:55.117 --> 08:57.495
W-Well, actually...

08:57.578 --> 08:58.454
Again?

08:58.538 --> 08:59.580
What did you do?

08:59.789 --> 09:05.336
Um, well, Eren gave us
a nice little gift, so then...

09:05.419 --> 09:07.964
Good work!

09:08.047 --> 09:09.799
I got you some refreshments.

09:09.882 --> 09:12.093
It's a cake made by Mr. Yoshida!

09:12.176 --> 09:13.094
Wow!

09:13.177 --> 09:16.138
So where are the trapdoors?

09:16.222 --> 09:18.766
Please, tell me about
the treasure chests, too!

09:20.226 --> 09:21.143
Oh, you see...

09:21.310 --> 09:23.271
I mean, what could I do?!

09:23.354 --> 09:28.276
I can't resist the allure of cake, and Master
Veldora and Milim say it won't be a problem!

09:28.359 --> 09:29.819
You're firing back at me?

09:30.403 --> 09:32.405
<i>It was straight-up bribery.</i>

09:32.488 --> 09:34.991
<i>I didn't know corruption
could happen this quickly.</i>

09:35.825 --> 09:39.036
But oh well, she only knows
about stuff on Floor 1.

09:39.120 --> 09:42.665
The chests with the real top-shelf
prizes weren't on that level.

09:42.748 --> 09:47.044
Team Kaval is doing a good job
landing treasure, don't they?

09:47.128 --> 09:51.465
I heard chests can sometimes be
found in small side rooms and the like.

09:51.549 --> 09:55.303
But some of them also have traps,
so you need to watch out for those as well.

09:55.386 --> 09:58.431
There are three types of treasure
chests in all; gold, silver, and bronze.

09:58.514 --> 10:01.434
It seems only the bronze chests run
the chance of being booby-trapped.

10:01.517 --> 10:04.353
So the gold chests is what
you really want, I suppose?

10:04.437 --> 10:07.857
Yes, apparently, those only
show up on floor numbers

10:07.940 --> 10:11.152
that are a multiple of ten-
the boss chambers.

10:11.235 --> 10:12.987
What do you mean by that?

10:13.070 --> 10:17.908
As all of you know, Sir Bovix has
been appointed the guardian of Floor 50.

10:17.992 --> 10:20.911
Likewise, we have other
"boss monsters" positioned

10:20.995 --> 10:23.581
in chambers in front
of the exit stairway.

10:23.664 --> 10:27.043
The gold chests are only for those Adventurers
who can defeat such formidable foes.

10:27.126 --> 10:29.170
And from those chest...

10:29.253 --> 10:34.967
You can get Rare-level...
Rare-level weapons and armor!

10:35.051 --> 10:37.428
<i>It's like a late-night infomercial show.</i>

10:37.637 --> 10:40.306
<i>I'm almost ashamed to be one
of those who came up with it.</i>

10:40.389 --> 10:42.224
<i>It worked like a charm, though.</i>

10:42.308 --> 10:46.062
I imagine most people here got to
see Bovix's strength for themselves.

10:46.228 --> 10:49.315
I'd love to see those proud of their
strength to take up the challenge.

10:49.398 --> 10:55.613
And one more thing, as you can see on the
screens, each floor is very large in size.

10:55.696 --> 11:00.785
So if you wanted to conquer the dungeon,
be prepared to take several days to do it.

11:00.868 --> 11:03.537
There are only bronze chests on Floor 1.

11:03.704 --> 11:06.040
You didn't mess around
with the contents, did you?

11:06.123 --> 11:08.000
All good there!

11:08.084 --> 11:09.251
Then good.

11:09.418 --> 11:14.006
Eren's textbook method still serve
as a good advertisement, after all.

11:14.215 --> 11:15.883
By the way, how about Masayuki?

11:15.966 --> 11:18.010
And look at this! Incredible!

11:18.094 --> 11:22.348
Team Lightspeed already
made their way to Floor 3!

11:22.431 --> 11:27.353
Living up to their name, Team Lightspeed
is making a lightspeed progress!

11:27.937 --> 11:32.024
Why?! It hasn't even been 30 minutes
and they're already on Floor 3?!

11:36.070 --> 11:41.575
And look at that! They made use
of the trapdoor and got to Floor 4!

11:41.659 --> 11:44.870
Masayuki! Masayuki!

11:44.954 --> 11:47.540
Didn't they laugh at Basson for
the same thing just a while ago?

11:47.623 --> 11:49.417
It is incredibly unfair.

11:50.000 --> 11:54.088
<i>You didn't tell me there'd be
this much trapdoors, Rimuru.</i>

11:54.463 --> 11:58.050
Looks like there are monsters on
the corridors from this floor onwards.

12:01.220 --> 12:03.222
Let's go!

12:03.597 --> 12:07.143
Now, as for Gaiye who went in solo...

12:07.226 --> 12:11.230
Whoa! He's dashing through the dungeon
with an incredible speed!

12:11.313 --> 12:15.860
He's currently on Floor 2 and is
about to reach the next stair down.

12:16.068 --> 12:18.195
He's heading straight to the stair,
not getting lost.

12:18.404 --> 12:21.365
Is he using a magic or something
to get information on his location?

12:21.615 --> 12:22.491
<i>Answer.</i>

12:22.575 --> 12:25.411
<i>This is the effect of
elemental magic Automap.</i>

12:25.578 --> 12:26.620
I see.

12:26.704 --> 12:28.956
So it is that magic that
display positional data into

12:29.039 --> 12:31.667
your brain, sort of like what
the Great Sage did for me.

12:31.876 --> 12:34.503
So he's not only a master swordsman,
but he can also use magic?

12:34.795 --> 12:37.173
He is an A-rank.
A rare breed, after all.

12:37.256 --> 12:41.635
At this pace, I believe he'd reach
Floor 5 within the time limit.

12:41.719 --> 12:42.553
Yeah.

12:42.636 --> 12:44.013
But still...

12:48.267 --> 12:51.103
Gaiye got to treasure chests
one after another!

12:51.187 --> 12:54.982
And it's all silver chests, too like
he knew where they were all along!

12:55.065 --> 12:57.151
He's he doing that?

12:58.360 --> 13:00.404
<i>Not even Raphael knows?</i>

13:01.363 --> 13:05.618
It's like that Gaiye guy got this intense
greed pushing him forward, y'know?

13:05.701 --> 13:09.079
Yeah, I wish I won't have
to get involved with him.

13:11.415 --> 13:13.792
Well done reaching this far,
you insignificant insects!

13:13.876 --> 13:17.671
Not a single one of you will
escape the Storm Dragon!

13:22.301 --> 13:25.387
Should I try sounding more solemn?

13:25.804 --> 13:28.390
Khahaha! Well done reaching this far-

13:35.105 --> 13:37.942
All member of the party
has been incapacitated.

13:38.442 --> 13:40.486
I'm returning them to the entrance.

13:42.863 --> 13:47.326
Whoa! Team Great Thunder
is back to square one!

13:48.536 --> 13:49.912
Would you like to retry?

13:49.995 --> 13:51.914
Y-Yeah! Of course!

13:53.582 --> 13:55.376
How many times does this makes now?

13:55.459 --> 13:58.921
They all got taken down
by sleeping gas trap just earlier.

13:59.004 --> 14:00.339
How bad can they be?

14:00.673 --> 14:03.884
By the way, is Eren's
team still on Floor 1?

14:03.968 --> 14:06.387
They're almost <i>too</i> cautious.

14:06.470 --> 14:09.431
We gathered enough potions now.
It's time, right?

14:09.515 --> 14:10.683
Are we really going?

14:10.766 --> 14:11.600
Do I have a right to sa-

14:11.684 --> 14:12.977
Let's go!

14:13.060 --> 14:16.146
Time to get the big fish!

14:16.397 --> 14:19.692
Look at that! Team Kaval
seems to be making their move!

14:25.281 --> 14:27.700
Taking a turn from
their thorough approach,

14:27.783 --> 14:30.077
they're now heading
straight to the deeper floors.

14:30.160 --> 14:32.329
Eren!

14:32.413 --> 14:36.584
Hmm, perhaps they're aiming to
get even better treasure chests?

14:36.667 --> 14:39.545
Can find Rare items from silver chests, too?

14:39.628 --> 14:42.381
Yes, but it's not something
you can aim for, really.

14:42.464 --> 14:46.176
Sir Gaiye has opened something
like twenty silver chests so far,

14:46.260 --> 14:48.053
but he still hasn't scored any Rares.

14:48.137 --> 14:51.682
So you'll need to look for gold chests
to get guaranteed Rare items?

14:51.765 --> 14:52.892
That's correct.

14:52.975 --> 14:58.272
But you can only find gold chests in the
designated boss-monster chambers, or...

14:58.355 --> 14:59.899
Are they anywhere else?

14:59.982 --> 15:04.153
There are other powerful creatures called
"area bosses" that you may run into at random.

15:04.236 --> 15:09.199
The rooms they guard
could contain golden chests.

15:09.283 --> 15:10.117
Hey, Ramiris.

15:10.200 --> 15:11.035
Yes, sir?

15:11.493 --> 15:15.873
Did you leak out the locations
of the area bosses as well?

15:15.956 --> 15:17.124
Well, um...

15:17.207 --> 15:18.250
Well?

15:18.334 --> 15:21.462
I-I think such a thing might
have been included, yes!

15:21.754 --> 15:23.547
Oh goodness...

15:23.797 --> 15:25.633
<i>Well, let's be optimistic.</i>

15:25.716 --> 15:27.843
<i>I think there are some
nasty monsters there,</i>

15:27.927 --> 15:31.096
<i>but if they saw them coming, I suppose
they could prepare for it well enough.</i>

15:33.307 --> 15:35.893
Wow. I'm shocked. It's Giant Bats.

15:35.976 --> 15:38.520
Don't panic. Kaval, I'm counting on you.

15:38.604 --> 15:40.898
I don't want them
sucking my blood, though...

15:40.981 --> 15:43.901
<i>They sound a little unnatural, but fine.</i>

15:45.778 --> 15:47.321
Here I go!

15:50.115 --> 15:52.826
Icicle Shot!

15:57.957 --> 15:59.959
Th-That was close.

16:00.167 --> 16:02.378
Eren! You're the best-

16:02.461 --> 16:03.545
Shut your mouth.

16:03.754 --> 16:06.966
Hmm, perhaps I made it a little too easy?

16:07.049 --> 16:07.925
Yeah.

16:08.008 --> 16:12.846
If this were Basson's party,
I bet it'd be a battle of life-and-death.

16:12.930 --> 16:16.350
But it won't be right to have Eren's party
as our baseline, wouldn't it?

16:16.433 --> 16:18.018
Like you have any right to say that!

16:20.854 --> 16:22.189
Looks like a sword...

16:22.272 --> 16:23.107
A sword?!

16:23.190 --> 16:25.859
Argh, I wanted some sorcerer's armor!

16:25.943 --> 16:26.902
Sweet!

16:26.986 --> 16:29.905
The heavens must be
watching how hard I'm working!

16:30.114 --> 16:31.615
Tempest Sword?!

16:31.699 --> 16:34.284
That's not just any Rare!
It's essentially a Unique!

16:34.576 --> 16:36.120
This feel like a waste now.

16:36.203 --> 16:39.373
Oh, they really got a weapon, Mjöllmile!

16:39.456 --> 16:41.208
Of course they did!

16:41.291 --> 16:46.338
The Demon Lord Rimuru has given me word
that every gold chest is a guaranteed hit.

16:51.802 --> 16:52.803
We're back!

16:52.886 --> 16:58.142
Oh! Team Kaval made their return
well before the time limit!

16:58.225 --> 16:59.768
Good work down there!

16:59.852 --> 17:03.439
We got some treasures,
and it was a lot of fun!

17:03.522 --> 17:07.067
Sheesh, they really only have
their eyes on the money.

17:07.151 --> 17:10.279
Eren, I'm so glad you
made it back safely...

17:10.362 --> 17:12.698
Do you think we can
at least make it that far?

17:12.781 --> 17:14.867
And we'll be back okay
even if we died.

17:14.950 --> 17:17.578
We'll also get magicrystal
if we defeat monsters!

17:17.661 --> 17:20.122
That alone will be enough
to make up the cost!

17:20.205 --> 17:22.374
All right! Let's go try it out next time!

17:22.458 --> 17:23.292
Yeah!

17:23.375 --> 17:25.794
<i>Well, at least it makes
a good advertisement.</i>

17:25.878 --> 17:32.342
Look at that! Meanwhile, Team Lightspeed
already made their way down to Floor 10!

17:32.551 --> 17:35.137
There should be a boss monster in this floor.

17:35.220 --> 17:37.389
It sure seems like it.

17:37.473 --> 17:39.683
Let's show them our power.

17:39.767 --> 17:41.185
Y-Yeah.

17:50.694 --> 17:53.739
Masayuki, leave this to me!

18:03.457 --> 18:05.834
Masayuki, I did it!

18:05.918 --> 18:09.296
W-Wow! He took down
a boss monster in an instant!

18:22.643 --> 18:25.521
The party is back with us,
along with a Rare item!

18:25.604 --> 18:29.066
So fast! No lies in the name "Lightspeed"!

18:29.608 --> 18:32.444
Remove all the trapdoors
in the upper floors.

18:32.528 --> 18:36.990
Oh, looks like Sir Gaiye is going
to challenge the earlier boss!

18:41.703 --> 18:44.123
That cursed Hero beat me here, eh?

18:44.414 --> 18:47.835
What happens in a situation like this, Mjöllmile?

18:47.918 --> 18:52.131
Well, I'm told that the boss is resurrected
in approximately thirty minutes.

18:52.214 --> 18:54.007
And the gold treasure chest with it?

18:54.091 --> 18:56.009
That's what I was told, yes.

18:56.093 --> 18:58.720
Otherwise, Great Rimuru
was concerned people

18:58.804 --> 19:01.932
would start fighting each
other to tackle a boss.

19:02.015 --> 19:03.600
I see, I see.

19:04.017 --> 19:05.894
Tch, fine.

19:06.270 --> 19:09.523
Hey! Get this boss back here now!

19:10.941 --> 19:13.360
There are 15 minutes left
before the time limit.

19:13.443 --> 19:14.361
Would you like to continue?

19:14.444 --> 19:18.240
Don't you screw with me!
Hurry up and resurrect the boss!

19:18.323 --> 19:21.201
The boss will be resurrected
in 28 minutes.

19:21.451 --> 19:23.120
It'll be past the time limit.

19:23.203 --> 19:29.543
There's no need at all for me to
abide by the rules of you buffoons!

19:31.712 --> 19:33.964
Clear rule violation confirmed.

19:34.131 --> 19:36.133
Executing punishment.

19:36.216 --> 19:38.051
Hmph, punishment?

19:38.135 --> 19:40.262
What could someone
like you could do to-

19:42.347 --> 19:43.932
These mere vines...

19:44.766 --> 19:47.895
I'll remove the pain suppressor effect
on your Resurrection Bracelet.

19:50.981 --> 19:54.568
Damn you! You think
that's all it takes to beat me?

19:54.651 --> 19:56.111
Final warning.

19:56.195 --> 19:57.863
Do you have any interest in apologizing?

19:57.946 --> 19:58.822
The hell I do!

19:59.406 --> 20:02.367
This level of magic could never-

20:06.622 --> 20:07.789
You're kidding me...

20:07.873 --> 20:09.958
She instantly kill Gaiye, an A-rank?

20:10.334 --> 20:14.463
<i>A dryad is already
above A-rank since birth.</i>

20:14.546 --> 20:18.175
<i>Plus, she receives training from Treyni
and others, so it's a foregone conclusion.</i>

20:18.258 --> 20:21.178
Oh, Gaiye has been resurrected!

20:21.261 --> 20:26.141
But, what's this?
He seems to be unconscious.

20:26.225 --> 20:30.938
The pain suppression effect on his Resurrection
Bracelet were turned off, after all.

20:31.021 --> 20:34.399
If you ignore the rules, you will receive
a punishment like the one you just saw,

20:34.483 --> 20:37.986
and you'll will be stripped
of the items you'd acquired!

20:38.153 --> 20:40.989
But in other words, as
long as you follow the rules,

20:41.073 --> 20:43.909
the Resurrection Bracelet
always works perfectly.

20:43.992 --> 20:46.495
We wish all Adventurers to
not fight among themselves,

20:46.578 --> 20:51.583
wait their turn, and conquer
this dungeon the right way.

20:54.253 --> 20:56.755
Um, by the way, how's
Team Great Lightning doing?

21:02.552 --> 21:04.513
All right! That's all!

21:10.686 --> 21:13.981
So what did you all think?
Did you have fun?

21:14.439 --> 21:18.819
We plan to officially open
this dungeon in the near future.

21:19.403 --> 21:21.405
I guarantee to all of you that it's safe,

21:21.488 --> 21:24.408
so please give it a try if you're interested.

21:25.200 --> 21:29.329
And for those who made their
their way to the hundredth floor...

21:30.080 --> 21:33.041
I will grant them the right
to challenge me to battle!

21:36.378 --> 21:40.549
<i>And with that, the dungeon
unveiling event came to a close.</i>

21:42.843 --> 21:47.222
<i>We cap off the final night of the
festival with a massive banquet.</i>

21:49.391 --> 21:52.102
<i>Everyone seemed to be having fun.
I couldn't ask for more.</i>

22:04.364 --> 22:08.452
<i>Over in town, all the stores were opened up
for free, letting not only its residents,</i>

22:08.535 --> 22:13.373
<i>but also merchants, adventurers, and farmers
to drink, sing, and have all the fun they can.</i>

22:15.500 --> 22:19.671
Monsters, humans- They equally
all dance and enjoyed the night.

22:20.922 --> 22:23.592
<i>It'd be great if this peaceful
moments could go on forever.</i>

22:26.011 --> 22:29.056
<i>It feels a little sad to see
the festival coming to an end.</i>

22:29.139 --> 22:32.184
<i>It almost feel like waste
to let it end here.</i>

22:34.019 --> 22:38.523
<i>But we have our works
waiting for us tomorrow.</i>

22:41.777 --> 22:43.111
<i>In the morning,
the following day...</i>

22:43.195 --> 22:45.947
<i>There is one large
task left for me to do.</i>

22:46.865 --> 22:48.408
<i>Yes, that is...</i>

22:48.742 --> 22:51.161
<i>The gold coin payment due date!</i>

24:26.256 --> 24:28.967
Next time, "After the Festival."
